# convert — ImageMagick image conversion

## Resize

```sh
# Fixed width, proportional height
convert original-image.jpg -resize 100x converted-image.jpg

# Fixed height, proportional width
convert original-image.jpg -resize x100 converted-image.jpg

# Fit within 100x100 (keeps aspect ratio)
convert original-image.jpg -resize 100x100 converted-image.jpg
```

## Resize and change file type at once

```sh
convert original-image.jpg -resize 100x converted-image.png
```

## Batch: resize every image in a directory

```sh
for file in original/image/path/*; do
    new_file=$(basename "${file%.*}")
    convert "$file" -resize 150 converted/image/path/"$new_file".png
done

# Or in place with mogrify (careful — overwrites!)
mogrify -resize 1920x *.jpg
```

## Real-world: thumbnails for the photo library

```sh
mkdir -p ~/Media/Photos/thumbs
for f in ~/Media/Photos/Phone/*.jpg; do
    convert "$f" -resize 400x -quality 85 ~/Media/Photos/thumbs/"$(basename "$f")"
done
```

## Real-world: quality, rotation, format

```sh
convert scan.png -quality 80 scan.jpg          # compress
convert photo.jpg -rotate 90 photo-rot.jpg     # rotate
convert page1.png page2.png doc.pdf            # images -> PDF
```

Note: on newer ImageMagick 7 installs the command is `magick` (`magick convert ...` also works).

| Flag      | What it does                |
| --------- | --------------------------- |
| -resize   | geometry WxH, W x, or xH    |
| -quality  | JPEG/PNG quality (1-100)    |
| -rotate   | degrees clockwise           |
| -strip    | drop EXIF metadata          |
